    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0870" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg788"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Judd</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 9, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to thank you for your despatch of
                    April 16, No. 62, which contains a very interesting exposition of the political
                    situation of western Europe. Since it arrived I have received news of the fall
                    of Duppel, which, doubtless, lends a new complexion to the war between Denmark
                    and Germany.</p>
                <p>I am advised that Mr. Corwin, availing himself of a leave of absence granted in
                    August last, expected to take his departure from Vera Cruz on the 3d instant.
                    The late accounts from Mexico show that the French forces have encountered
                    several reverses; but the statements are not very minute, and everything that
                    comes from that quarter, in the interest of either belligerent, is believed to
                    be much exaggerated. Nothing that has occurred there or in Europe has been
                    thought to furnish sufficient ground for a change of the attidude which the
                    United States has hitherto held in regard to Mexico.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman B. Judd</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., Berlin</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
